    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C15"],
      "claim": "Tropane analogs such as AHN 1-055 and JHW 007 readily crossed the BBB with brain-to-plasma ratios at least 2-fold higher than cocaine, supporting robust CNS access for this chemotype.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C10"],
      "claim": "A tropane PET ligand in humans rapidly entered the brain and distributed to receptor-rich regions, confirming meaningful CNS access in humans for tropane derivatives.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C03"],
      "claim": "N-methylated azabicyclic/piperidine esters showed rapid high brain uptake of about 10% dose/g at 1 min in mice, indicating sufficient lipophilicity and BBB penetration for this ester class.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C19"],
      "claim": "Diphenhydramine, a basic lipophilic amine with a brain-to-plasma ratio of 18.4 and no Pgp efflux, supports that similar basic lipophilic molecules can achieve high CNS exposure.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "The query is an N-methyl tropane ester with a phenyl and hydroxymethyl side chain, closely related to multiple tropane-based CNS PET ligands and esters that show rapid, high brain uptake across species. All high-transfer experimental evidence supports BBB penetration; therefore predict pass.",
